msgid "Transpile an LUCJ ansatz {#transpile-an-lucj-ansatz}"
msgstr "Transpiler un ansatz LUCJ {#transpile-an-lucj-ansatz}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The concepts in this guide are only available in the Python API.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Les concepts de ce guide ne sont disponibles que dans l'API Python.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The local unitary cluster Jastrow ([LUCJ](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlelanding/2023/sc/d3sc02516k)) ansatz is a compact, hardware-efficient parametrization of a correlated electronic wavefunction. It is a member of the more general unitary cluster Jastrow (UCJ) family and takes the form\n"
msgstr "L'ansatz de Jastrow à clusters unitaires locaux ([LUCJ](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlelanding/2023/sc/d3sc02516k)) est une paramétrisation compacte et efficace pour le matériel d'une fonction d'onde électronique corrélée. C'est un membre de la famille plus générale de Jastrow à clusters unitaires (UCJ) et il prend la forme\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\Psi \\rangle = \\left(\\prod_{k=1}^{L} \\mathcal{U}_k\\, e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}\\,\n"
"\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger\\right) \\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\Psi \\rangle = \\left(\\prod_{k=1}^{L} \\mathcal{U}_k\\, e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}\\,\n"
"\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger\\right) \\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle$ is a reference state (typically Hartree-Fock), each $\\mathcal{U}_k$ is an orbital rotation, and each $\\mathcal{J}_k$ is a diagonal Coulomb operator\n"
msgstr "où $\\lvert \\Phi_0 \\rangle$ est un état de référence (typiquement Hartree-Fock), chaque $\\mathcal{U}_k$ est une rotation d'orbitales, et chaque $\\mathcal{J}_k$ est un opérateur de Coulomb diagonal\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{J} = \\frac12 \\sum_{ij,\\sigma\\tau} \\mathbf{J}^{\\sigma\\tau}_{ij}\\,\n"
"n_{i\\sigma}\\, n_{j\\tau},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{J} = \\frac12 \\sum_{ij,\\sigma\\tau} \\mathbf{J}^{\\sigma\\tau}_{ij}\\,\n"
"n_{i\\sigma}\\, n_{j\\tau},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with $n_{i\\sigma}$ the number operator on spatial orbital $i$ with spin $\\sigma$.\n"
msgstr "avec $n_{i\\sigma}$ l'opérateur nombre sur l'orbitale spatiale $i$ de spin $\\sigma$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) builds the ansatz operator; this package turns it into a circuit and lowers that circuit onto qubits. This guide is about the second half of that sentence. The reason to make the trip is the lowering itself: ffsim’s own Qiskit gates are specific to the Jordan-Wigner transformation, whereas a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") carries no assumption about its fermion-to-qubit encoding, so the same ansatz can be synthesized through whichever encoding suits the target device.\n"
msgstr "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) construit l'opérateur d'ansatz ; ce paquet le transforme en circuit et abaisse ce circuit sur des qubits. Ce guide porte sur la seconde moitié de cette phrase. La raison de faire le détour est l'abaissement lui-même : les portes Qiskit propres à ffsim sont spécifiques à la transformation de Jordan-Wigner, alors qu'un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") ne fait aucune hypothèse sur son encodage fermion-vers-qubit, de sorte que le même ansatz peut être synthétisé avec l'encodage qui convient au dispositif cible.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ansatz operator therefore arrives here ready-made, and everything below is what happens to it afterwards: what the gate decomposes into, how it lowers through Jordan-Wigner, how it is matched to a device coupling map, and what a non-Jordan-Wigner lowering would still need. For building, parametrizing, or simulating a UCJ ansatz in the first place, see ffsim’s [own guides](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/how-to-guides/qiskit-lucj.html).\n"
msgstr "L'opérateur d'ansatz arrive donc ici tout prêt, et tout ce qui suit décrit ce qui lui arrive ensuite : en quoi la porte se décompose, comment elle s'abaisse via Jordan-Wigner, comment elle est adaptée à la carte de couplage d'un dispositif, et ce dont un abaissement non Jordan-Wigner aurait encore besoin. Pour construire, paramétrer ou simuler un ansatz UCJ en premier lieu, consulte les [guides propres](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/how-to-guides/qiskit-lucj.html) de ffsim.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"See also\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The [ffsim relationship guide](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation) for how the two packages divide the work, and the [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) for the pipeline stages used below.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Voir aussi\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Le [guide de la relation avec ffsim](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation) pour savoir comment les deux paquets se partagent le travail, et le [guide de transpilation](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) pour les étapes du pipeline utilisées ci-dessous.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"get-an-lucj-operator-from-ffsim\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Get an LUCJ operator from ffsim {#1-get-an-lucj-operator-from-ffsim}"
msgstr "1. Obtenir un opérateur LUCJ depuis ffsim {#1-get-an-lucj-operator-from-ffsim}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ansatz is initialized from the amplitudes of a coupled-cluster singles and doubles (CCSD) calculation. Run restricted Hartree-Fock followed by CCSD for a hydrogen molecule in the `6-31g` basis, using [PySCF](https://pyscf.org/) for the quantum chemistry, then hand the amplitudes to ffsim’s [`from_t_amplitudes()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.from_t_amplitudes \"(in ffsim)\"). It performs a *double factorization* of the $t_2$ amplitudes to obtain the per-layer diagonal Coulomb matrices and orbital rotations, and derives an optional final orbital rotation from the $t_1$ amplitudes. The number of repetitions $L$ is whatever that factorization yields; `n_reps` truncates it, trading accuracy for a shallower circuit.\n"
msgstr "L'ansatz est initialisé à partir des amplitudes d'un calcul coupled-cluster avec simples et doubles (CCSD). Exécute un Hartree-Fock restreint suivi d'un CCSD pour une molécule d'hydrogène dans la base `6-31g`, en utilisant [PySCF](https://pyscf.org/) pour la chimie quantique, puis passe les amplitudes à [`from_t_amplitudes()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.from_t_amplitudes \"(in ffsim)\") de ffsim. Cette fonction effectue une *double factorisation* des amplitudes $t_2$ pour obtenir les matrices de Coulomb diagonales et les rotations d'orbitales de chaque couche, et déduit une rotation d'orbitales finale facultative à partir des amplitudes $t_1$. Le nombre de répétitions $L$ est ce que donne cette factorisation ; `n_reps` le tronque, échangeant de la précision contre un circuit moins profond.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is where the ansatz stops being an ffsim concern. ffsim offers choices here that this package neither sees nor needs to know about, such as the variationally optimized (“compressed”) factorization behind `optimize=True`, or the parameter-vector packing that a variational optimizer drives. All of them produce the same kind of operator, and everything below works unchanged on any of them.\n"
msgstr "C'est ici que l'ansatz cesse d'être une affaire de ffsim. ffsim propose ici des choix que ce paquet ne voit pas et n'a pas besoin de connaître, comme la factorisation optimisée de façon variationnelle (« compressée ») derrière `optimize=True`, ou l'empaquetage du vecteur de paramètres que pilote un optimiseur variationnel. Tous produisent le même type d'opérateur, et tout ce qui suit fonctionne sans changement sur n'importe lequel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"turn-the-operator-into-a-fermionic-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Turn the operator into a fermionic circuit {#2-turn-the-operator-into-a-fermionic-circuit}"
msgstr "2. Transformer l'opérateur en circuit fermionique {#2-turn-the-operator-into-a-fermionic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") gate wraps the operator and expresses it as a circuit over *fermionic modes*. The gate is a pure unitary carrying no reference of its own, so prepend an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate (built with [`from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\")) to supply the Hartree-Fock reference the ansatz is applied to.\n"
msgstr "La porte [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") enveloppe l'opérateur et l'exprime comme un circuit sur des *modes fermioniques*. La porte est un unitaire pur sans référence propre, donc ajoute en tête une porte [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") (construite avec [`from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\")) pour fournir la référence Hartree-Fock à laquelle l'ansatz est appliqué.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Decomposing the circuit reveals its anatomy, and this is the representation the rest of the guide operates on. The [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate prepares the reference determinant, and each ansatz layer contributes an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") $\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger$, then $e^{i\\mathcal{J}_k}$ (an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") of the diagonal Coulomb operator $\\mathcal{J}_k$), then $\\mathcal{U}_k$, with a final [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") at the end. The orbital rotations act per spin sector, so each is placed on the alpha modes `0..norb` and the beta modes `norb..2*norb` independently.\n"
msgstr "Décomposer le circuit révèle son anatomie, et c'est la représentation sur laquelle opère le reste du guide. La porte [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") prépare le déterminant de référence, et chaque couche de l'ansatz apporte une [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") $\\mathcal{U}_k^\\dagger$, puis $e^{i\\mathcal{J}_k}$ (une [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") de l'opérateur de Coulomb diagonal $\\mathcal{J}_k$), puis $\\mathcal{U}_k$, avec une [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") finale à la fin. Les rotations d'orbitales agissent par secteur de spin, chacune est donc placée indépendamment sur les modes alpha `0..norb` et les modes bêta `norb..2*norb`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The gates that the UCJ ansatz decomposes into.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/lucj-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The gates that the UCJ ansatz decomposes into.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/lucj-3.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every gate in that decomposition is still fermionic: [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") and [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") are defined on modes, and no qubit or Pauli operator has appeared yet. That is what leaves the encoding open, and it is the state the ansatz stays in until the synthesis stage picks one.\n"
msgstr "Chaque porte de cette décomposition est encore fermionique : [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") et [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") sont définies sur des modes, et aucun opérateur de qubit ou de Pauli n'est encore apparu. C'est ce qui laisse l'encodage ouvert, et c'est l'état dans lequel l'ansatz reste jusqu'à ce que l'étape de synthèse en choisisse un.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Each layer ends with $\\mathcal{U}_k$ and the next begins with $\\mathcal{U}_{k+1}^\\dagger$, so adjacent [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates could be merged into a single rotation. A transpilation pass performing this fusion is a planned future development.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Remarque\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Chaque couche se termine par $\\mathcal{U}_k$ et la suivante commence par $\\mathcal{U}_{k+1}^\\dagger$, de sorte que des portes [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") adjacentes pourraient être fusionnées en une seule rotation. Une passe de transpilation réalisant cette fusion est un développement futur prévu.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"choose-a-fermion-to-qubit-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Choose a fermion-to-qubit encoding {#3-choose-a-fermion-to-qubit-encoding}"
msgstr "3. Choisir un encodage fermion-vers-qubit {#3-choose-a-fermion-to-qubit-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit is still fermionic, and that is the point at which this package earns its place in the workflow. A [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") carries no assumption about how modes become qubits, so the encoding is a *synthesis-stage* choice rather than something baked into the ansatz. That is what this package adds over ffsim’s own Qiskit gates, which are specific to the Jordan-Wigner transformation.\n"
msgstr "Le circuit est encore fermionique, et c'est le point où ce paquet gagne sa place dans le workflow. Un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") ne fait aucune hypothèse sur la façon dont les modes deviennent des qubits, l'encodage est donc un choix de *l'étape de synthèse* plutôt que quelque chose d'intégré à l'ansatz. C'est ce que ce paquet apporte par rapport aux portes Qiskit propres à ffsim, qui sont spécifiques à la transformation de Jordan-Wigner.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For Jordan-Wigner alone you would not need this detour: ffsim ships [`UCJOpSpinBalancedJW`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW.html#ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW \"(in ffsim)\") and its siblings, which take a UCJ operator to a qubit circuit on their own. The reason to route the ansatz through a fermionic circuit is everything *else* an encoding can buy you. Local encodings, for instance, spend extra qubits to bound the Pauli weight of each term, which the [1D](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) and [2D](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) flow-set guides use to make a Trotter step’s two-qubit depth independent of the system size.\n"
msgstr "Pour Jordan-Wigner seul, tu n'aurais pas besoin de ce détour : ffsim fournit [`UCJOpSpinBalancedJW`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW.html#ffsim.qiskit.UCJOpSpinBalancedJW \"(in ffsim)\") et ses équivalents, qui transforment seuls un opérateur UCJ en circuit de qubits. La raison de faire passer l'ansatz par un circuit fermionique est tout ce que *d'autre* un encodage peut t'apporter. Les encodages locaux, par exemple, dépensent des qubits supplémentaires pour borner le poids de Pauli de chaque terme, ce que les guides d'ensembles de flux [1D](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) et [2D](2-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) utilisent pour rendre la profondeur à deux qubits d'un pas de Trotter indépendante de la taille du système.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a UCJ ansatz specifically, the synthesis stage has to cover two kinds of gate:\n"
msgstr "Pour un ansatz UCJ en particulier, l'étape de synthèse doit couvrir deux types de portes :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The diagonal Coulomb evolution.** [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") is already encoding-agnostic: [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") takes a mapper function, so the $e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}$ layers lower through any encoding you can express as one. The [flow-set guides](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) show how to write one.\n"
msgstr "**L'évolution de Coulomb diagonale.** [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") est déjà indépendante de l'encodage : [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") prend une fonction de mapper, de sorte que les couches $e^{i \\mathcal{J}_k}$ s'abaissent via tout encodage que tu peux exprimer ainsi. Les [guides d'ensembles de flux](1-d-fermi-hubbard#d-fermi-hubbard) montrent comment en écrire une.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The orbital rotations and the Slater-determinant preparation.** Neither an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") nor the [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") that the leading [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") and rotation fuse into (see below) is mapped to qubits as such. The [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") pass first breaks them down, in fermionic space, into [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gates on one or two modes each (and, for the preparation, an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") of the reference), so any encoding that can map an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") handles them. Under Jordan-Wigner, the factors between adjacent modes become [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)objects at the qubit stage.\n"
msgstr "**Les rotations d'orbitales et la préparation du déterminant de Slater.** Ni une [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") ni la [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") dans laquelle fusionnent l'[`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") initiale et la rotation (voir plus bas) ne sont mappées telles quelles sur des qubits. La passe [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") les décompose d'abord, dans l'espace fermionique, en portes [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") sur un ou deux modes chacune (et, pour la préparation, une [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") de la référence), de sorte que tout encodage capable de mapper une [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") les gère. Sous Jordan-Wigner, les facteurs entre modes adjacents deviennent des objets [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)à l'étape des qubits.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The initialization.** The plugin for [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") is not parametrized by an encoding: it documents its assumption of an occupation-basis encoding with a 1-to-1 mode-to-qubit mapping, and emits gates directly on that basis. A different encoding needs its own plugin for it, and none ships yet.\n"
msgstr "**L'initialisation.** Le plugin pour [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") n'est pas paramétré par un encodage : il documente son hypothèse d'un encodage en base d'occupation avec une correspondance 1-pour-1 entre modes et qubits, et émet directement des portes dans cette base. Un autre encodage nécessite son propre plugin, et aucun n'est encore fourni.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to transpile UCJ circuits under a non-Jordan-Wigner encoding is an open research question and this package provides the framework within which to develop such a pipeline. The remainder of this guide constructs the transpiler pipeline for the Jordan-Wigner encoding, equivalent to the one produced by [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\"), as an example.\n"
msgstr "La façon de transpiler des circuits UCJ sous un encodage autre que Jordan-Wigner est une question de recherche ouverte, et ce paquet fournit le cadre dans lequel développer un tel pipeline. Le reste de ce guide construit, à titre d'exemple, le pipeline de transpilation pour l'encodage de Jordan-Wigner, équivalent à celui produit par [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\").\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"lower-it-through-jordan-wigner\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Lower it through Jordan-Wigner {#4-lower-it-through-jordan-wigner}"
msgstr "4. L'abaisser via Jordan-Wigner {#4-lower-it-through-jordan-wigner}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lowering happens in [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\"), which works like Qiskit’s [`HighLevelSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.HighLevelSynthesis): it walks the fermionic instructions and hands each to a plugin registered for that gate name. Its [`F2QSynthesis.methods`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis.methods \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis.methods\") attribute holds one [`F2QSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-f-2-q-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.F2QSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.F2QSynthesisPlugin\") per gate name, so building the stage means choosing a plugin for every fermionic gate the circuit contains:\n"
msgstr "L'abaissement a lieu dans [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\"), qui fonctionne comme la [`HighLevelSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.HighLevelSynthesis) de Qiskit : elle parcourt les instructions fermioniques et confie chacune à un plugin enregistré pour ce nom de porte. Son attribut [`F2QSynthesis.methods`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis.methods \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis.methods\") contient un [`F2QSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-f-2-q-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.F2QSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.F2QSynthesisPlugin\") par nom de porte, donc construire l'étape revient à choisir un plugin pour chaque porte fermionique que contient le circuit :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assigning instances like this is also how a plugin you wrote yourself enters the pipeline, without having to register it anywhere first.\n"
msgstr "Affecter des instances de cette façon est aussi la manière d'intégrer au pipeline un plugin que tu as écrit toi-même, sans avoir à l'enregistrer au préalable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is where the encoding is settled, in the two ways section 3 described: explicitly, by handing [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") to [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\"), and implicitly, by the other plugin already assuming it.\n"
msgstr "C'est ici que l'encodage est fixé, des deux façons décrites à la section 3 : explicitement, en passant [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") à [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\"), et implicitement, par l'autre plugin qui le suppose déjà.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That stage then slots into a [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager) whose stages run in a fixed order:\n"
msgstr "Cette étape s'insère ensuite dans un [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager) dont les étapes s'exécutent dans un ordre fixe :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **optimization** stage runs *before* synthesis, on the fermionic circuit, which is what makes it worth having: it rewrites gates while they are still fermionic and encoding-agnostic, so the savings carry to whatever encoding follows. [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") collapses each run of consecutive [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates into one, which matters for a UCJ ansatz because every layer ends with $\\mathcal{U}_k$ and the next begins with $\\mathcal{U}_{k+1}^\\dagger$. [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") then fuses the leading [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") and the rotation that follows it into a single [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"), which synthesis lowers through the cheaper reduced Slater decomposition instead of a full square rotation. The order matters: merging the rotations first exposes the single rotation immediately after the initialization, which the Slater fusion then contracts into it. [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") comes last, because it breaks up whatever rotation is left, and doing so any earlier would leave the two merging passes with nothing to fuse.\n"
msgstr "L'étape d'**optimisation** s'exécute *avant* la synthèse, sur le circuit fermionique, ce qui la rend précieuse : elle réécrit les portes tant qu'elles sont encore fermioniques et indépendantes de l'encodage, de sorte que les gains se transmettent à l'encodage qui suit. [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") réduit chaque suite de portes [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") consécutives à une seule, ce qui compte pour un ansatz UCJ car chaque couche se termine par $\\mathcal{U}_k$ et la suivante commence par $\\mathcal{U}_{k+1}^\\dagger$. [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") fusionne ensuite l'[`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") initiale et la rotation qui la suit en une seule [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"), que la synthèse abaisse via la décomposition de Slater réduite, moins coûteuse, au lieu d'une rotation carrée complète. L'ordre compte : fusionner d'abord les rotations expose la rotation unique immédiatement après l'initialisation, que la fusion de Slater absorbe ensuite. [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") vient en dernier, car elle découpe toute rotation restante, et le faire plus tôt ne laisserait rien à fusionner aux deux passes de fusion.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The remaining stages are plumbing. `input` and `output` convert between circuits and DAGs, `layout` assigns fermionic modes to qubits ([`TrivialF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-trivial-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout\") maps mode `i` to qubit `i`), and `qubit` is an ordinary Qiskit pass manager that takes over once nothing fermionic is left.\n"
msgstr "Les étapes restantes sont de la tuyauterie. `input` et `output` convertissent entre circuits et DAG, `layout` affecte les modes fermioniques aux qubits ([`TrivialF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-trivial-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.TrivialF2QLayout\") associe le mode `i` au qubit `i`), et `qubit` est un pass manager Qiskit ordinaire qui prend le relais une fois qu'il ne reste plus rien de fermionique.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running it requires one preparatory step: the composite [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") gate has to be decomposed into its primitive gates first, so the optimization stage can see the individual rotations and evolutions.\n"
msgstr "L'exécuter demande une étape préparatoire : la porte composite [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") doit d'abord être décomposée en ses portes primitives, afin que l'étape d'optimisation puisse voir les rotations et évolutions individuelles.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Without a target device, this maps onto `2 * norb` qubits with all-to-all connectivity assumed; the orbital rotations synthesize into [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)objects and the diagonal Coulomb evolutions into [`RZZGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RZZGate)objects:\n"
msgstr "Sans dispositif cible, cela se mappe sur `2 * norb` qubits avec une connectivité supposée totale ; les rotations d'orbitales se synthétisent en objets [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)et les évolutions de Coulomb diagonales en objets [`RZZGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RZZGate):\n"

